  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GEO: Building the Capacity of Civil Society to Mitigate Election Crises</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The 2024 Georgia parliamentary elections present an important opportunity for Georgian democratic stakeholders to strengthen electoral integrity, prevent democratic backsliding, and reduce corrosive dialogue. The International Foundation for Electoral Systems will partner with local civil society organisations to bolster their ability to navigate and adapt to Georgia&#x2019;s challenging and fluid political environment; engage with citizens and stakeholders; and deliver meaningful oversight of political actors and electoral processes. The International Foundation for Electoral Systems will provide training on elections technology; tailored information and education for voters; and enhanced civil society organisations capacity to identify and respond to electoral crises approaches ahead of the 2024 parliamentary elections.</narrative>
  </description>
